From 71410eb36ac0e099dc207cc85a713d085636233e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Root <jacob@otisroot.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 02:25:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: buffer input into libinput during blocking DRM ioctls

Blocking modesets (DPMS on, ~hundreds of ms each on nvidia) and the forced
connector probes run on every hotplug uevent (~200ms per connector on nvidia)
stall the compositor's main thread. Meanwhile the kernel's per-device evdev
buffer (64 events, ~10 keystrokes) overflows: libinput reports SYN_DROPPED
and typed keys are lost - e.g. a password typed into the lock screen while
the monitors wake.

Run those ioctls on a helper thread and keep calling libinput_dispatch() on
the main thread until they return. That only moves kernel events into
libinput's own growable queue; they are handled afterwards by the normal
dispatch (scheduled as an idle event, since the fd no longer polls readable).
---
